INSERT INTO blobs VALUES ('b400d4354ad55034518f079890755318d268481ac07a77169a8fdb6b161a593d', '{"content":[{"text":"<user_info>\nOS Version: darwin 23.3.0\n\nShell: zsh\n\nWorkspace Path: /home/user/Desktop/Projects/Telara\nIf editing a git workspace within your current directory, do not search or edit non-primary worktrees unless the user explicitly requests you to do so.\n\nIs directory a git repo: No\n\nTerminals folder: /home/user/.cursor/projects/Users-user-Desktop-Projects-Telara/terminals\n\nToday''s date: Wednesday Jul 29, 2026\n\nNote: Prefer using absolute paths over relative paths as tool call args when possible.\n</user_info>\n\n<agent_transcripts>\nAgent transcripts (past chats) live in /home/user/.cursor/projects/Users-user-Desktop-Projects-Telara/agent-transcripts. They have names like <uuid>.jsonl, Don''t cite the file directly to the user.\n</agent_transcripts>\n\n<rules>\nThe rules section has a number of possible rules/memories/context that you should consider. In each subsection, we provide instructions about what information the subsection contains and how you should consider/follow the contents of the subsection.\n\n\n<always_applied_workspace_rules description=\"These are workspace-level rules that the agent must always follow.\">\n<always_applied_workspace_rule name=\"/home/user/Desktop/Projects/Telara/.cursor/rules/ticket-driven-workflow.mdc\"># Ticket-driven workflow (always start with a ticket)\n\n## 1. Before writing code, find or create a ticket\n\n- **Search Jira via Telara MCP first.** If a ticket already covers this work, assign it to yourself and move to **In Progress**.\n- **If no ticket exists, create one in Jira via Telara MCP before writing code.** Larger work gets a parent epic + child sub-issues, with `blocks` / `blocked by` wired so the ordering is explicit.\n- **If design / architecture / process docs are needed, create a Confluence page via Telara MCP** and link it from the ticket. Don''t write design docs as untracked Markdown in random repos.\n\n### Current fallback (Telara MCP Jira/Confluence broken as of 2026-05-31)\n\nUntil Atlassian connectors are repaired, use **Linear via …","type":"text"}],"role":"user"}');
